This is an independently implemented, idiomatic Java port of the owner's SpecQR
QR Code Model 2 algorithms and contracts. It is not a wrapper around a different
language, QR library, native encoder, or service. Runtime dependencies: java.base.

Primary contract baseline:
SpecQR/SpecQR 15ad15e5c770ea0e39072f8f88b2733018f02ffd (v3.0.0-rc.2), MIT.
Additional owner-authored port references:
SpecQR/SpecQR-Python 1deb5cf83ed7a93eeb44138e5980a963a00cdffb, MIT.
SpecQR/SpecQR-Swift 0ef9613fe8f1ecd687da76ce797b4ef896afa477, MIT.
SpecQR/SpecQR-CSharp 057c4b3f25e52c4786a8f94c744ff884eedcecfa, MIT.
SpecQR/SpecQR-CPP e91cd8fe4434fd6ef10d1126bb2fd17b0b19321f, MIT.
SpecQR/SpecQR-Conformance-Lab 72ad78c979327e3e261526ea3c0a164efa4ab390, MIT.

Independent encoders/decoders are used only by development verification tools.
No third-party QR implementation source or bytecode is included in the library.
